## N.M. Yingwani (220122253)

**Project Role:** Database Administrator

**Features Implemented:**
- Complete MySQL schema with 15 tables
- Stored procedures for common queries
- Triggers for automatic daily usage aggregation
- Views for dashboard statistics
- Foreign key cascade design

**Tests Written:**
- Data integrity tests
- Foreign key cascade verification

**Bugs Identified and Corrected:**
- BUG-006 (verify-email null guard)

**Relevant Commits:**
- e8c1a56 - fix: guard against null currentUser in verify-email page

**Reflection:**
Designing the dual-database architecture was challenging because Firebase and MySQL have fundamentally different data models. I settled on using the Firebase UID as the common key and adding sync flags to track synchronization status. The cascade delete behaviour ensures that deleting a user in MySQL does not leave orphaned records, but I had to coordinate this with the Firebase Admin SDK deletion. Understanding when to trust the relational layer and when to trust the document layer was the biggest lesson of the sprint.

