- BUG-011 (hardcoded date string)

**Relevant Commits:**
- (commit hash for the WiFi credential fix)
- (commit hash for the NTP time fix)

**Reflection:**
The most surprising challenge was network reliability. The ESP32 needs to buffer readings during WiFi outages and batch-upload them when the connection restores. This shaped our decision to use Firebase's push method, which generates time-ordered keys and allows later offline uploads to slot correctly into the timeline. Getting NTP working on the ESP32 also revealed how easy it is to accidentally hardcode time values and how much damage that can do to historical data.

