**Reflection:**
Building the automated test result generator taught me that testing tools are as important as the tests themselves. A failing test that does not produce actionable output is useless. The edge cases including empty strings, whitespace-only passwords, and extreme values revealed several validation gaps that we then fixed. The most valuable lesson was that a test suite is only as good as its assertions. Using strict equality versus loose equality matters when checking data types, and understanding PHP's arithmetic behaviour prevented a lot of confusion.

